  "worked_solution": "To graph the first inequality $y\\ge 2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x.$\n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x.$ \n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/6190eb782fb731535c261e85e11fa5e20b3894c3602ed94a834ba5b2dd752135.png)",
